WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.921
The prize ceremony produces a clear picture of discovery, with

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:09.292
a handful of faces attached to a complicated scientific history.

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:18.905
Experiments accumulate through earlier questions, technical adaptations, overlooked

00:00:18.905 --> 00:00:23.967
collaborators and results that sometimes become useful years later.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:33.573
A manuscript records coauthors, while a method may depend on

00:00:33.573 --> 00:00:38.013
technicians, students and predecessor teams who never enter the headline.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:47.901
Every selection tells us whom an institution has chosen to remember.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:53.127
Historical recognition is never identical to an exhaustive chain of contribution.

00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:02.898
An inclusive account cannot simply invent forgotten heroes. It must

00:01:02.898 --> 00:01:07.412
return to papers, notebooks, patents and who actually did the work.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:16.147
The essay asks for better histories of discovery

00:01:16.147 --> 00:01:20.244
without denying that major scientific contributions deserve recognition.
